<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Defines if the demandMultiplier ratio has already been applied to the associated quantities or not.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Boolean</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o1079">
<a:ObjectID>5E67D4CA-DB85-446F-BDFB-5C2E8ACDE1C3</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>demandMultiplier</a:Name>
<a:Code>demandMultiplier</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>An additional multiplier that may be used for normalization of the demand value to an hourly value.  For example, if the demand interval were set to 15 minutes, the demand multiplier would be 4.  If the meter design is such that the demand value reported and displayed is compensated for by the meter itself and no additional scaling is required outside of the meter, the value of the demand multiplier should be &quot;1&quot;.
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Float</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
