<o:Class Id="o754">
<a:ObjectID>D37C317F-EA32-4F6A-913C-914F0720ECC5</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>MeterComModule</a:Name>
<a:Code>MeterComModule</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>An AMR (automated meter reading) module is configured within a meter asset to support communication with an AMR system. Where a meter asset may only have the basic capability to measure usage, an AMR module often can augment the capabilites of the meter to provide for more advanced capabilities such as time of use, outage detection, load control, tamper detection, etc., as well as providing for two way communications with an AMR master station.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o1117">
<a:ObjectID>8C22291B-03EF-4346-898C-70ED9C42D058</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>amrAddress</a:Name>
<a:Code>amrAddress</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The communication ID number (e.g. serial number, IP address, telephone number, etc.) of the AMR module which serves this meter.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o1118">
<a:ObjectID>677222F5-6F24-4BE0-B83A-159616EED904</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>amrRouter</a:Name>
<a:Code>amrRouter</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The communication ID number (e.g. port number, serial number, data collector ID, etc.) of the parent device associated to this AMR module.

Note: The thought here is that if someone swaps out a meter, they may inadvertently disrupt the AMR system. Some technologies route readings from nearby meters through a common collection point on an electricity meter. Removal of such a meter disrupts AMR for numerous nearby meters. 
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o1119">
<a:ObjectID>9EF0AC56-3559-4E6A-B940-3D1F0D4584CF</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>oneWay</a:Name>
<a:Code>oneWay</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>This field is set to TRUE indicate if the AMR module can only send, but can not receive messages.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Boolean</a:DataType>
<a:InitialValue>1</a:InitialValue>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o1120">
<a:ObjectID>34A5AB6B-91CC-4053-A367-722FDB6842F0</a:ObjectID>
