<a:Comment>Whereas an AssetModel is a particular model and version of a vendor&#39;r product, a TypeAsset is documentation for a generic asset that may be used for design purposes.  Any number of AssetModels may be used to perform this generic function.  The primary role of the TypeAsset is typically defined by the PowereSystemResource it is associated with</a:Comment>
