<o:Attribute Id="o1761">
<a:ObjectID>1751DF53-FDC5-43DD-A6CC-054E1368AE48</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>bil</a:Name>
<a:Code>bil</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Basic Insulation Level (BIL) for switchgear, insulators, etc. 
A reference insulation level expressed as the impulse crest voltage of a nominal wave, typically 1.2 X 50 microsecond.  This is a measure of the ability of the insulation to withstand very high voltage surges. 
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Voltage</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o1762">
<a:ObjectID>32AD7B06-0B70-4CB9-9FAB-1C627DE7ABC0</a:ObjectID>
