<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o2365">
<a:ObjectID>29563C6B-EB5C-4AAD-9FE4-91ADA6703CF2</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>ErpPersonLocationRole</a:Name>
<a:Code>ErpPersonLocationRole</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Roles played between People and Locations.  Some Locations are somewhat static, like the person&#39;s home address.  Other locations may be dynamic, for example when the person is part of a crew driving around in truck.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o2366">
<a:ObjectID>54925C12-A829-4A66-A9FA-03BF9F890410</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>PersonPropertyRole</a:Name>
<a:Code>PersonPropertyRole</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The role of a person relative to a given piece of property.  Examples of roles include: owner, renter, contractor, etc.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o2361">
<a:ObjectID>867A3159-DEDD-4CF3-9A9E-3A16663DE084</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>OrgPropertyRole</a:Name>
<a:Code>OrgPropertyRole</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Roles played between Organisations and a given piece of property.  For example, the Organisation may be the owner, renter, occupier, taxiing authority, etc.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o2372">
<a:ObjectID>ECC6E9A2-5987-424F-9039-6A150FBD60D1</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Hazard</a:Name>
<a:Code>Hazard</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A hazard is any object or condition that is a danger for causing loss or perils to an asset and/or people.  Examples of hazards are trees growing under overhead power lines, a park being located by a substation (i.e., children climb fence to recover a ball), a lake near an overhead distribution line (fishing pole/line contacting power lines), etc.  </a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
