<o:Class Id="o2513">
<a:ObjectID>4E3D0A33-FC40-4586-AEFB-3214592CC7F0</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>DocLocRole</a:Name>
<a:Code>DocLocRole</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Roles played between Documents and Locations.  For example, as ErpAddress is a type of Location and WorkBilling is a type of Document, a role is the address for which to mail the invoice.  As a TroubleTicket is a type of Document, one instance of Location may be the address for which the trouble is reported.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o2515">
<a:ObjectID>5F4ADCBC-C641-47C4-9DBA-D726D674F055</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Craft</a:Name>
<a:Code>Craft</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A person, such as a member of a crew, must have necessary knowledged and skills in one or more crafts before being allowed to perform certain types of work.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o2517">
<a:ObjectID>2387F8E9-75E7-4273-A1E6-CE8C4185E6F0</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>OrgLocationRole</a:Name>
<a:Code>OrgLocationRole</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Roles played between Organisations and Locations, for example a service territory or school district.  Note that roles dealing with use of a specific piece of property should be defined based on the relationship between OccupationsOfProperty and Location.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o2518">
<a:ObjectID>27536841-AD12-4794-9614-9BE5F4334B7C</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Assignment</a:Name>
<a:Code>Assignment</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>An assignment is given to an ErpPerson, Crew, Organisation, Equipment Item, Tool, etc. and may be used to perform Work, WorkTasks, Procedures, etc.  TimeSchedules may be set up directly for Assignments or indirectly via the associated WorkTask.  Note that these associations are all inherited through the recursive relationship on Document.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
