<c:Classes>
<o:Class Id="o3188">
<a:ObjectID>9C19810C-248A-4E10-BCDC-CCD49452DD43</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>ChangeSet</a:Name>
<a:Code>ChangeSet</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The updates required in a transaction for an existing data set are grouped into a single ChangeSet.  In data sets (e.g., NetworkDataSet), each major step in the ChangeSet is described through a separate ChangeItem associated with the data set.  Within each data set, each inidividual object change is described with a seperate ChangeItem associated with the object.  </a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o3189">
<a:ObjectID>5DA27042-33E8-4117-B87E-B3D0E5215451</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>NetworkDataSet</a:Name>
<a:Code>NetworkDataSet</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Categorized as a type of document, a network data set is a model of a portion of the electrical network that includes a list of the equipment, along with relevant connectivity, electrical characteristics, geographical location, and various parameters associated with the equipment.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o3192">
<a:ObjectID>B5BE3089-AD8E-459F-9AB8-0F92D82DED2E</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>LandBase</a:Name>
<a:Code>LandBase</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Land base data.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o3187">
<a:ObjectID>7BD9A9D9-7184-4B7D-9F5F-69C444AA14B9</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>LoadDataSet</a:Name>
<a:Code>LoadDataSet</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Customer, supply point or area load data.  May include Meter records for customers (where regulations allow).</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o3190">
<a:ObjectID>2CCDD5E8-126D-4F04-89ED-9E8E96160EB3</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Circuit</a:Name>
<a:Code>Circuit</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A static collection of conducting equipment originating at a main distribution center and supplying one or more secondary distribution centers, one or more branch-circuit distribution centers, or any combination of these two types of equipment.  It is the source to the next normally open point.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o3207">
<a:ObjectID>918F2384-2F1B-4BF4-B2FE-673E11EBDFF2</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>code</a:Name>
<a:Code>code</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The code for this circuit.  Some companies use this attribute to identify the circuit colour used for reference by operators, draftsmen, etc. on displays, maps, etc.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o3208">
<a:ObjectID>F7AD34B6-A99F-4489-968D-B5C2E2D3DA90</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>ratedKV</a:Name>
<a:Code>ratedKV</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Rated (not actual) voltage of the circuit.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Voltage</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o3193">
<a:ObjectID>23D52B3C-A79D-4F2D-832B-7AA21578737C</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>ChangeItem</a:Name>
<a:Code>ChangeItem</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The change type (add, delete, modify) and sequence number for this change within a set of changes.  The changes for this change item are articulated in an instances of data sets, lists, catalogues, and other message types.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o3209">
<a:ObjectID>E0020ADA-8503-435D-A07E-D44D1FAD6F3E</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>changeType</a:Name>
<a:Code>changeType</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Type of change for the associated object: add, delete, modify.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o3210">
<a:ObjectID>D7C72B6C-90A2-414D-A4DD-F5A6D0958878</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>sequenceNum</a:Name>
<a:Code>sequenceNum</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Relative order of this change in an ordered sequence of changes.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o3191">
<a:ObjectID>009E97D3-C8EC-4984-A9FF-1D9573B020A2</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>CircuitSection</a:Name>
<a:Code>CircuitSection</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A section of circuit located between two sectionalizing devices.  A circuit section may contain other circuit sections, for example, a lateral tapped off a primary.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
