<o:Class Id="o3267">
<a:ObjectID>236F78FE-D528-462E-B925-3C0C3D42FBF8</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>OperationalRestriction</a:Name>
<a:Code>OperationalRestriction</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>An Operational Restriction is a type of document that can be associated with a device to describe any sort of restrictions compared with the original manufacturer&#39;s specification e.g. temporary maximum loadings, maximum switching current, do not operate if bus couplers are open etc etc. 
In the UK, for example, if a breaker or switch ever mal-operates, this is reported centrally and utilities use their asset systems to identify all the installed devices of the same manufacturer&#39;s type. They then apply operational restrictions in the operational systems to warn operators of potential problems. After appropriate inspection and maintenance, the operational restrictions may be removed.

</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
