<c:Classes>
<o:Class Id="o3360">
<a:ObjectID>80EB1D72-A80A-46A2-B57D-804414AE762A</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>OutageRecord</a:Name>
<a:Code>OutageRecord</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment> A document describing details of an outage in part of the electrical network. Typically produced  by a SCADA system following a breaker trip or within a Trouble Call System by grouping customer calls. This has an associated OutageStep for each supply point.

In some countries all outage restoration is performed using a SwitchingSchedule which complements the OutageRecord and records the ErpPersons (crew) and any planned Work. In other systems, it may be acceptable to manage outages including new WorkTasks without switching schedules.
Note: The relationship between OutageRecord and ErpPerson and Crew is inherited as each is a type of Document.
</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o3367">
<a:ObjectID>B1732BBF-F1F1-4D95-973E-5B111FA5E69C</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>outageType</a:Name>
<a:Code>outageType</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment> Type of outage, often express as a cause code.  While many cause codes may be applicable to a given outage, the primary cause in captured here.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>EnumeratedType</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o3368">
<a:ObjectID>B4A7AEF1-958C-4E4A-A66B-A34BEBFB5F81</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>endDateTime</a:Name>
<a:Code>endDateTime</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Time restoration was completed for all customers impacted by this outage.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>AbsoluteDateTime</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o3369">
<a:ObjectID>81D3FDA3-1482-4038-BBC7-61251DEA824C</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>isPlanned</a:Name>
<a:Code>isPlanned</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment> false if unplanned, for example due to a breaker trip.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>boolean</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o3370">
<a:ObjectID>DF6294B0-D990-4056-BCCD-65EEB56B229A</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>startDateTime</a:Name>
<a:Code>startDateTime</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment> date and time first customer went off-supply</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>AbsoluteDateTime</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o3371">
<a:ObjectID>93515B77-0242-4B89-A0FF-FB396ED64780</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>currentStatus</a:Name>
<a:Code>currentStatus</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Current status of the overall outage.  Note that each status change is recorded in an associated Activity Record.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o3372">
<a:ObjectID>C7FD222A-48C3-4775-95D6-3CC3C4DF5DEE</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>actionTaken</a:Name>
<a:Code>actionTaken</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Overall action taken to resolve outage.  Reference associated work tasks for details.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o3373">
<a:ObjectID>69325642-E406-460B-A36C-9F38897172CE</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>damageCode</a:Name>
<a:Code>damageCode</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The damage code relative to the associated PowerSystemResource(s) and/or Asset(s). Examples include broken, burnout, failure, flashed (burned), manually operated, wire down, no damage - rolling blackout, none. </a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o3374">
<a:ObjectID>F9C8FF15-3030-4732-8772-65E62050854A</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>mode</a:Name>
<a:Code>mode</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The value of Organisation.mode at the time of OutageRecord.startDateTime.  Some utilities use text to describe various modes like nominal, storm, emergency, other.  Other utilities use severity ratings where, for example, 0 is a nominal condition and 5 is the most severe condition.  This information is often required for outage reporting purposes.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o3359">
<a:ObjectID>7386577D-C99D-46FA-9BB9-CD181B516274</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>OutageReport</a:Name>
<a:Code>OutageReport</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment> A document describing the statistics related to an outage.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o3375">
<a:ObjectID>828F8441-22F0-4161-A0D9-F7B326DCBF37</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>totalCustomers</a:Name>
<a:Code>totalCustomers</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment> Number of customers for the Outage Record</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Integer</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o3376">
<a:ObjectID>BC2CEA7C-40A4-43DB-9905-6A3D56531D9B</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>totalDuration</a:Name>
<a:Code>totalDuration</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment> Total outage time.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Integer</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o3377">
<a:ObjectID>2B956D19-5BF9-4220-9A42-5B4DC09F8669</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>aveCustomerMinsLost</a:Name>
<a:Code>aveCustomerMinsLost</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The average cusotmer minutes of interruption for this outage.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Integer</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o3378">
<a:ObjectID>B326996C-882C-4014-925C-3BC322632E4E</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>totalCustomerMinsLost</a:Name>
<a:Code>totalCustomerMinsLost</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Total minutes of customer interruption.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Integer</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o3358">
<a:ObjectID>1ACE6827-A1EE-4580-80A3-1A5F1A0B564F</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>OutageStep</a:Name>
<a:Code>OutageStep</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Holds an Outage History (start time, end time) for each supply point of an outage record.   The supply point for a given step is the associated PowerSystemResource instance.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o3379">
<a:ObjectID>C69A4BC4-C465-4859-9FC4-4F16FEF92153</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>offDateTime</a:Name>
<a:Code>offDateTime</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Time power was lost.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>AbsoluteDateTime</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o3380">
<a:ObjectID>0D4C1785-FE46-4BDD-8116-2AB43A1BE28B</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>onDateTime</a:Name>
<a:Code>onDateTime</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
