<a:Comment>Bank ABA</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o3900">
<a:ObjectID>9EE92636-53B7-4601-886E-4D01B28DF2FF</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>ErpJournal</a:Name>
<a:Code>ErpJournal</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A book for recording accounting transactions as they occur.  Transactions and adjustments are first recorded in a journal, which is like a diary of instructions, advising which account to be charged and by how much.

A journal represents a change in the balances of a business&#39;s financial accounts.  Many tasks or transactions throughout an enterprise will result in the creation of a journal.  Some examples are creating a customer invoice, paying a vendor, transferring inventory, or paying employees.
</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
