<c:Classes>
<o:Class Id="o5197">
<a:ObjectID>50AD8E16-7415-4DB7-B6DE-C9E7354C5210</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>GmlFeatureStyle</a:Name>
<a:Code>GmlFeatureStyle</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Styling features means styling a particular aspect or aspects of a feature. We can style feature geometry, topology or display arbitrary text string. </a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o5230">
<a:ObjectID>DF38D622-BCBF-4345-9753-EE762D97682E</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>version</a:Name>
<a:Code>version</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>In order that that the version numbers can be identified when the SLD pieces are used independently.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5231">
<a:ObjectID>E804471E-F46D-46BF-A4DC-99AAA645D142</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>featureTypeName</a:Name>
<a:Code>featureTypeName</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Identifies the specific feature type that the feature-type style is for.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5232">
<a:ObjectID>3DFDDF1D-98BF-439E-8868-AC130C9BF63B</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>semanticTypeIdentifier</a:Name>
<a:Code>semanticTypeIdentifier</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The SemanticTypeIdentifier is experimental in GML and is intended to be used to identify what the feature style is suitable to be used for using community-controlled name(s). For example, a single style may be suitable to use with many different feature types.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5233">
<a:ObjectID>E32911AA-7D1D-4D5A-B4A6-9AE8F834DA09</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>queryGrammar</a:Name>
<a:Code>queryGrammar</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The value of this property which is defined as an enumeration specifies the grammar that is used in the content of the gml:featureConstraint element The enumeration allows for three values: Xpath, Xquery and other.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5234">
<a:ObjectID>96019AD5-762D-4ADE-9C09-2A9092DB5D3F</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>featureConstraint</a:Name>
<a:Code>featureConstraint</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>This property is used to further constrain the feature instance set to which the style applies. It is optional and it&#39;s value is an XPath expression. If the property does not exist, the style applies to all feature instances selected by featureType or baseType attribute.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5235">
<a:ObjectID>F210DB38-270B-4D7A-B8F7-EB097A9706BB</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>featuretype</a:Name>
<a:Code>featuretype</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The simplest and most common way of relating features and styles is by using this attribute. It’s value will be the declared name of a feature, instances of which we want to style. For example, if the value is Switch, the FeatureStyle object will simply apply to all Switch features. </a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5236">
<a:ObjectID>102FC6B1-1A62-40E5-B3FE-961CE55F4F1C</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>basetype</a:Name>
<a:Code>basetype</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Another way of selecting the feature instances to which the style applies is to specify, as the value of this attribute, the name of the base type from which feature or features derive. </a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o5193">
<a:ObjectID>29025216-59B0-4BA5-B90A-F6C75129D80C</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>GmlGeometryStyle</a:Name>
<a:Code>GmlGeometryStyle</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>GeometryStyle describes the style for one geometry of a feature. Any number of geometry style descriptors can be assigned to one feature style. This is usually required for features with multiple geometry properties.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o5237">
<a:ObjectID>D44F3725-C564-4E4D-8181-8E42B63661FE</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>geometryProperty</a:Name>
<a:Code>geometryProperty</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The geometryProperty attribute on the GeometryStyle class specifies the name of the geometry property of a feature to which this GeometryStyle applies. </a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5238">
<a:ObjectID>4078C48B-7EF6-4395-8D8A-E5420C4801C3</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>geometryType</a:Name>
<a:Code>geometryType</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>It is necessary to specify the geometry type using
geometryType attribute as well since the application schema of the geometry property may allow different
geometries as it&#39;s value.
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5239">
<a:ObjectID>BF324107-0894-4BF7-BAE2-7071D3DAAA3D</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>symbol</a:Name>
<a:Code>symbol</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The symbol element specifies a graphical symbol used to render a geometry or a topology. A symbol is a description of graphical attributes of a graphical object without a particular, implicit meaning. It can be a description of a line, circle, polygon or more complex drawing. </a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o5195">
<a:ObjectID>E0A33DD8-0BDA-44D3-A11A-07DD2A9898A4</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>GmlLabelStyle</a:Name>
<a:Code>GmlLabelStyle</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Describes the style for the text that is to be displayed along with the graphical representation of a feature. The content of the label is not necessarily defined in the GML data set. More precisely, the content can be static text specified in the style itself and the text from the GML data set. Label style has two elements: gml:style that specifies the style and gml:label that is used to compose the label content.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o5240">
<a:ObjectID>081135CD-D6AE-4927-97CB-18DD1B18346A</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>labelExpression</a:Name>
<a:Code>labelExpression</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Allows both text content and unbounded number of gml:LabelExpression elements. The value of gml:LabelExpression element is an XPath expression that selects the value of some property of the feature.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5241">
<a:ObjectID>54B44D94-8319-4F62-AC04-019897EB3175</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>style</a:Name>
<a:Code>style</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Used to specify the style of the rendered text. The CSS2 styling expressions grammar should be used to express graphic properties</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5242">
<a:ObjectID>84091845-406D-44AD-8075-ACB643315DE5</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>transform</a:Name>
<a:Code>transform</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Allows us to specify a transformation expression that will be applied to the symbol in the rendering phase. It&#39;s type is xsd:string and the value is specified in the SVG specification (transform attribute).</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o5194">
<a:ObjectID>2F257E56-171C-4E4F-993C-DB9772EB8E8A</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>GmlTopologyStyle</a:Name>
<a:Code>GmlTopologyStyle</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Describes the style for one topology property. Similarly to the Geometry style, a feature can have multiple topology properties, thus multiple topology style descriptors can be specified within one feature style.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o5199">
<a:ObjectID>FE4CED8B-6812-41F4-97C4-36D0E015E8B9</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>GmlSymbol</a:Name>
<a:Code>GmlSymbol</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A symbol describes how a feature is to appear on a map or display. The symbol describes not just the shape that should appear but also such graphical properties as color and opacity. </a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o5243">
<a:ObjectID>3D96AE55-D065-4A54-BC21-390CD1066423</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>version</a:Name>
<a:Code>version</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The version of the Symbol</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5244">
<a:ObjectID>4465E62C-EBE0-41AB-ADE6-E2A7A335C563</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>type</a:Name>
<a:Code>type</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The Symbol type</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5245">
<a:ObjectID>EDE5A9FC-9831-4906-8B62-9F7254FE926C</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>level</a:Name>
<a:Code>level</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The level (of the map) where the symbol exists or the zoom levels at which this diagram object is displayed.  As a way of de-cluttering displays, for example, some symbols and annotations are only shown when zoomed in.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o5187">
<a:ObjectID>5556D4C8-FA72-4BAE-AFFE-E6887B0A4596</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>RULE</a:Name>
<a:Code>RULE</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Rules are used to group rendering instructions by feature-property conditions and map scales.</a:Comment>
<a:Stereotype>GML</a:Stereotype>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o5211">
<a:ObjectID>4645DE1D-0CF8-4DE5-8925-E3CA07543A7D</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>GmlLineSymbol</a:Name>
<a:Code>GmlLineSymbol</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A LineSymbol is used to style a &quot;stroke&quot; along a linear geometry type, such as a string of line segments.
</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o5246">
<a:ObjectID>3E0BE8AE-3DB6-434F-A27D-150DAE503F3D</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>sourceSide</a:Name>
<a:Code>sourceSide</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>For dynamic network update (i.e. colouring) purposes</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>string</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o5212">
<a:ObjectID>660ECBAA-3C2A-44EA-B3F5-97E678F1E7DD</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>GmlPolygonSymbol</a:Name>
<a:Code>GmlPolygonSymbol</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Used to draw a polygon (or other area-type geometries), including filling its interior and stroking its border (outline).</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o5214">
<a:ObjectID>F790CAC9-4F51-4B0E-BD6D-606AD00A490D</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>GmlTextSymbol</a:Name>
<a:Code>GmlTextSymbol</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Used for styling text labels</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o5247">
<a:ObjectID>9E5EC8F0-A2D6-45D5-BB00-5915B087D62F</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>label</a:Name>
<a:Code>label</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Used to provide text-label content. If a Label value is not provided, then no text will be rendered.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5248">
<a:ObjectID>32D19D5A-8BC5-4A73-A5F6-F425589E1E53</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>labelType</a:Name>
<a:Code>labelType</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The type-classification of a label. The Label element is used to provide text-label content.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5249">
<a:ObjectID>624D19CC-9E13-43D0-B63C-960BC982051A</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>minFontSize</a:Name>
<a:Code>minFontSize</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment> The minimum font size allowed.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Integer</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5250">
<a:ObjectID>9654997B-12B4-4ED0-A309-73D873862797</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>property</a:Name>
<a:Code>property</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A &quot;TextSymbol&quot; is used to render text labels according to various graphical parameters. &quot;Property&quot; provides a generic method for capturing all unspecified information pertaining to the TextSymbol.
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5251">
<a:ObjectID>F4D023F7-992D-4931-8FBC-AC0424223076</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>fieldID</a:Name>
<a:Code>fieldID</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The name of the field of the class being annotated.  Most objects will include name, description, and aliasName.  Many objects may contain other fields such as comment, status, etc.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o5210">
<a:ObjectID>510EACE7-9FAC-430E-9EE2-D37D6BE2BB38</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>GmlPointSymbol</a:Name>
<a:Code>GmlPointSymbol</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A PointSymbol is used to draw a &quot;graphic&quot; at a point.
</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o5213">
<a:ObjectID>E86F5DDE-FF31-465E-8F8A-004DC97613FB</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>GmlRasterSymbol</a:Name>
<a:Code>GmlRasterSymbol</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Describes how to render raster/matrix-coverage data (e.g., satellite photos, DEMs).</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o5252">
<a:ObjectID>7AB317DB-8D41-4950-88C5-134B9AB40A60</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>opacity</a:Name>
<a:Code>opacity</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Specifies the level of translucency to use when rendering the Graphic.The value is encoded as a floating-point value
between 0.0 and 1.0 with 0.0 representing completely transparent and 1.0 representing completely opaque, with a linear scale of translucency for intermediate values. The default value is 1.0
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Float</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5253">
<a:ObjectID>0F20C931-816A-41B8-850A-0608A2A15547</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>overlapbehaviour</a:Name>
<a:Code>overlapbehaviour</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Tells a system how to behave when multiple raster images in a layer overlap each other, for example with  satellite-image scenes.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5254">
<a:ObjectID>F76D593F-B288-4A9D-95BF-F4732002178B</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>redSourcename</a:Name>
<a:Code>redSourcename</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Colour Channels are identified by a system and data-dependent character identifier. Contrast enhancement may be applied to each channel in isolation. </a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5255">
<a:ObjectID>4FE479D1-CFE9-4873-A6CE-217C3669CE1D</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>greenSourceName</a:Name>
<a:Code>greenSourceName</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Colour Channels are identified by a system and data-dependent character identifier. Contrast enhancement may be applied to each channel in isolation. </a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5256">
<a:ObjectID>D140F2A1-247D-496D-B1EA-F3CC39ABA6C9</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>blueSourcename</a:Name>
<a:Code>blueSourcename</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Colour Channels are identified by a system and data-dependent character identifier. Contrast enhancement may be applied to each channel in isolation. </a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5257">
<a:ObjectID>003B6132-3932-48A8-B959-4288C2AD1B7F</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>graySourcename</a:Name>
<a:Code>graySourcename</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A single colour channel may be selected to display in grayscale. Colour Channels are identified by a system and data-dependent character identifier. Contrast enhancement may be applied to each channel in isolation. </a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5258">
<a:ObjectID>66618B18-0089-40EA-AE3A-993AA2545BD3</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>brighnessOnly</a:Name>
<a:Code>brighnessOnly</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>If the BrightnessOnly flag is 0 (false, default), the shading is applied to the layer being rendered as the current RasterSymbol. If BrightnessOnly is 1 (true), the shading is applied to the brightness of the colors in the rendering canvas generated so far by other layers, with the effect of relief-shading these other layers. </a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Boolean</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5259">
<a:ObjectID>ED04DB9A-7818-4375-BEDB-6B2191C87341</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>reliefFactor</a:Name>
<a:Code>reliefFactor</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The ReliefFactor gives the amount of exaggeration to use for the height of the &quot;hills&quot;. A value of around 55 (times) gives reasonable results for Earth-based DEMs. The default value is system-dependent.
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o5204">
<a:ObjectID>E2E86E1A-FBA3-4A00-A2E7-2371DC546685</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>GmlStroke</a:Name>
<a:Code>GmlStroke</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The Stroke element encapsulates the graphical symbolization parameters for linear geometries.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o5260">
<a:ObjectID>BD41A5E2-CFA3-4D21-A8A0-AE4DD490EF5E</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>opacity</a:Name>
<a:Code>opacity</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Specifies the level of translucency to use when rendering the stroke. The value is encoded as a floating-point value
between 0.0 and 1.0 with 0.0 representing completely transparent and 1.0 representing completely opaque, with a linear scale of translucency for intermediate values. The default value is 1.0
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Float</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5261">
<a:ObjectID>4E201C85-004E-4017-AED4-93BF049B8D1F</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>width</a:Name>
<a:Code>width</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The absolute width (thickness) of a stroke in pixels encoded as a float. The default is 1.0. Fractional numbers are allowed (with a system-dependent interpretation) but negative numbers are not.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Float</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5262">
<a:ObjectID>4203708A-A98C-45E6-A142-C7D3A6340B31</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>linejoin</a:Name>
<a:Code>linejoin</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Enumerated values telling how line strings should be joined (between line segments). The values are represented as content strings.

The allowed values for line join are &quot;mitre&quot;, &quot;round&quot;, and &quot;bevel&quot;. The default values are system-dependent.
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5263">
<a:ObjectID>569F158D-B5BC-4ACE-BC14-687061C03A79</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>lineCap</a:Name>
<a:Code>lineCap</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Enumerated values telling how line strings should be capped (at the two ends of the line string). The values are represented as content strings.

The allowed values for line cap are &quot;butt&quot;, &quot;round&quot;, and &quot;square&quot;. The default values are system-dependent.
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5264">
<a:ObjectID>F2140C22-C648-40DA-889D-AE54BDB9008E</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>lineStyle</a:Name>
<a:Code>lineStyle</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The name of a defined line style. Usually will be an enumerated value and will be system-specific.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5265">
<a:ObjectID>660E9F66-37C9-4E92-8C50-B089938FB14D</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>dashArray</a:Name>
<a:Code>dashArray</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Encodes a dash pattern as a series of space separated floats. The first number gives the length in pixels of dash to draw, the second gives the amount of space to leave, and this pattern repeats. If an odd number of values is given, then the pattern is expanded by repeating it twice to give an even number of values. Decimal values have a system-dependent interpretation (usually depending on whether antialiasing is being used). The default is to draw an unbroken line.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5266">
<a:ObjectID>DA7628EB-1FD0-48F7-BE39-2AA67FED8884</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>dashOffset</a:Name>
<a:Code>dashOffset</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Specifies the distance as a float into the &quot;stroke-dasharray&quot; pattern at which to start drawing.
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o5205">
<a:ObjectID>2AF68144-DCD2-45E7-A95D-67D9CACC3DF2</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>GmlFill</a:Name>
<a:Code>GmlFill</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Specifies how the area of the geometry will be filled.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o5267">
<a:ObjectID>042B55EF-2CAE-494E-BA51-163087DE477F</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>opacity</a:Name>
<a:Code>opacity</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Specifies the level of translucency to use when rendering the Fill. The value is encoded as a floating-point value
between 0.0 and 1.0 with 0.0 representing completely transparent and 1.0 representing completely opaque, with a linear scale of translucency for intermediate values. The default value is 1.0
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Float</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o5208">
<a:ObjectID>87E3A67E-5A62-4E18-AA92-744D7DF32C17</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>GmlHalo</a:Name>
<a:Code>GmlHalo</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A Halo is a type of Fill that is applied to the backgrounds of font glyphs. The use of halos greatly improves the readability of text labels.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o5268">
<a:ObjectID>CCDE71BA-6596-4B29-8C9F-5C0EE549721D</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>radius</a:Name>
<a:Code>radius</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The Radius element gives the absolute size of a halo radius in pixels encoded as a floating-point number. The radius is taken from the outside edge of a font glyph to extend the area of coverage of the glyph (and the inside edge of “holes” in the glyphs). The default radius is one pixel. Negative values are not allowed.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5269">
<a:ObjectID>4886FADC-52C3-479C-8443-F57FC6972FCE</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>opacity</a:Name>
<a:Code>opacity</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Specifies the level of translucency to use when rendering the Fill. The value is encoded as a floating-point value
between 0.0 and 1.0 with 0.0 representing completely transparent and 1.0 representing completely opaque, with a linear scale of translucency for intermediate values. The default value is 1.0
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Float</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o5206">
<a:ObjectID>617E7683-697E-49EF-955C-5D3BF8844B9F</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>GmlFont</a:Name>
<a:Code>GmlFont</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Identifies a font of a certain family, style, and size.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o5270">
<a:ObjectID>88340DE3-8688-4E95-99B3-A45CCD4F339C</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>family</a:Name>
<a:Code>family</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Gives the family name of a font to use. Allowed values are system-dependent. Any number of font-family attributes may be given and they are assumed to be in preferred order.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5271">
<a:ObjectID>F6A1B274-7384-4DCE-9C07-F8FD8618D5B7</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>style</a:Name>
<a:Code>style</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The style to use for a font. The allowed values are &quot;normal&quot;, &quot;italic&quot;, and &quot;oblique&quot;.
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5272">
<a:ObjectID>1B042F76-48DD-4556-8161-1379106FB4A3</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>weight</a:Name>
<a:Code>weight</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The amount of weight or boldness to use for a font. Allowed values are &quot;normal&quot; and &quot;bold&quot;.
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5273">
<a:ObjectID>9611B750-D514-49EF-9A56-315E0BCDF359</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>size</a:Name>
<a:Code>size</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The size to use for the font in pixels. The default is defined to be 10 pixels, though various systems may have restrictions on what sizes are available.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5274">
<a:ObjectID>A293ECE8-1BBB-48B7-9E2F-2E69025EC4B3</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>absoluteSize</a:Name>
<a:Code>absoluteSize</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>True if &quot;size&quot; is expressed in absolute values.  Default is false.
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Boolean</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o5203">
<a:ObjectID>BEFBDEF0-688D-4792-8543-EDEF54AF467A</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>GmlGraphic</a:Name>
<a:Code>GmlGraphic</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A &quot;graphic symbol&quot; with an inherent shape, color(s), and possibly size. A &quot;graphic&quot; can be very informally defined as &quot;a little picture&quot; and can be of either a raster or vector-graphic source type.
</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o5275">
<a:ObjectID>EAD890FB-7F59-4B56-8F5A-4D4BCE7841B5</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>opacity</a:Name>
<a:Code>opacity</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Specifies the level of translucency to use when rendering the Graphic.The value is encoded as a floating-point value
between 0.0 and 1.0 with 0.0 representing completely transparent and 1.0 representing completely opaque, with a linear scale of translucency for intermediate values. The default value is 1.0
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Float</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5276">
<a:ObjectID>30374BDF-0BFF-4C44-8D7B-8C3D586E4AA2</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>size</a:Name>
<a:Code>size</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Gives the absolute size of the graphic in pixels encoded as a floatingpoint number. The default size for an object is context-dependent. Negative values are not allowed.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Integer</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5277">
<a:ObjectID>CC937AA2-D597-44FF-A383-77D13E7FFB44</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>minSize</a:Name>
<a:Code>minSize</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The minimum symbol size allowed.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Integer</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5278">
<a:ObjectID>045CD240-69A8-40ED-9C42-D1B41FEFA713</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>rotation</a:Name>
<a:Code>rotation</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Gives the rotation of a graphic in the clockwise direction about its center point in decimal degrees, encoded as a floating-point number. Negative values mean counter-clockwise rotation. The default value is 0.0 (no rotation). Note that there is no connection between source geometry types and rotations; the point used for plotting has no inherent direction. Also, the point within the graphic about which it is rotated is format dependent. If a format does not include an inherent rotation point, then the point of rotation should be the centroid.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>AngleDegrees</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5279">
<a:ObjectID>A642DB7B-0A3C-418E-9F07-7FFC8A41E32E</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>xScale</a:Name>
<a:Code>xScale</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Horizontal scaling factor of normal symbol - particularly applicable to busbars if not described through a sequence of gmlPositions (e.g., Busbar).</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Float</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5280">
<a:ObjectID>E915706E-43EC-46E3-9680-68968765F53D</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>yScale</a:Name>
<a:Code>yScale</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Vertical scaling factor of normal symbol - particularly applicable to busbars if not described through a sequence of gmlPositions (e.g., Busbars).</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Float</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5281">
<a:ObjectID>925E44A9-160A-4956-813D-BC909213281C</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>symbolID</a:Name>
<a:Code>symbolID</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The identifier of the symbol, if not derived from the type of CIM object (PSR, Asset, Organisation, Document, etc.) gmlSymbolPlacement is associated with.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>string</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o5200">
<a:ObjectID>C93BAE91-D2B7-4B6A-9E4A-8B066852190A</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>GmlMark</a:Name>
<a:Code>GmlMark</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Defines a &quot;shape&quot; which has coloring applied to it (i.e. square, circle, triangle, star, ...).
</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o5282">
<a:ObjectID>6FE837E5-B435-4769-9501-84F6AB893A0D</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>wellKnownName</a:Name>
<a:Code>wellKnownName</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Gives the well-known name of the shape of the mark.
Allowed values include at least square, circle, triangle, star, cross, and x.
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o5201">
<a:ObjectID>23101DE4-2D25-49AC-83B1-7BEA4FBB5410</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>GmlSvgParameter</a:Name>
<a:Code>GmlSvgParameter</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A &quot;SvgParameter&quot; refers to an SVG/CSS graphical-formatting parameter. The parameter is identified using the &quot;name&quot; attribute and the content of the element gives the SVG/CSS-coded value.
</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o5283">
<a:ObjectID>52C37B32-85BD-44EA-9047-FA6344F6EF31</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>VGAttribute</a:Name>
<a:Code>VGAttribute</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The sVGAttribute of the SvgParameter is defined here. (e.g for &quot;Stroke&quot;, the following SvgParameters may be used: &quot;stroke&quot; (color), &quot;stroke-opacity&quot;, &quot;stroke-width&quot;, &quot;stroke-linejoin&quot;, &quot;stroke-linecap&quot;, &quot;stroke-dasharray&quot;, and &quot;stroke-dashoffset&quot;. Others are not officially supported.)
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5284">
<a:ObjectID>0017990D-DEA3-4B77-9B73-AF3A73876A01</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>value</a:Name>
<a:Code>value</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The SVG/CSS-coded value of the associated SvgAttribute.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o5198">
<a:ObjectID>89E7D8FC-4C13-4FA4-BDF9-6B9195B229BA</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>GmlBaseSymbol</a:Name>
<a:Code>GmlBaseSymbol</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The BaseSymbol class allows referencing &amp; extension of external symbols, which may be stored in a symbol repository. The graphical properties from a referenced external symbol override the ones read in from the base symbol.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o5207">
<a:ObjectID>5AD0A8AA-ADE9-4DB4-8B52-802072F84F34</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>GmlLabelplacement</a:Name>
<a:Code>GmlLabelplacement</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Used to position a label relative to a point or a line
string
</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o5285">
<a:ObjectID>E70DF6E8-DD7D-4BBE-8004-4290715AEB66</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>typeLabelPlace</a:Name>
<a:Code>typeLabelPlace</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The type of &quot;LabelPlacement&quot; which in turn specifies where and how a text label should be rendered relative to a geometry.
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5286">
<a:ObjectID>E476EE58-46C6-476A-9D65-BDFBC07946AE</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>displacementX</a:Name>
<a:Code>displacementX</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Gives the X displacement from the main-geometry point to render a text label</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5287">
<a:ObjectID>9EBEE29B-9D2D-4420-842D-4889277F80AC</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>displacementY</a:Name>
<a:Code>displacementY</a:Code>
