<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Free text name of the object or instance. </a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5532">
<a:ObjectID>7F254A04-35D9-45D8-A82C-FB087A1ABB29</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>description</a:Name>
<a:Code>description</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The description is an arbitrary human readable text describing or naming the object. It may be non unique and may not correlate to a naming hierarchy.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5533">
<a:ObjectID>899E5FCD-5AA5-4CCB-B35F-048A75ED1CC8</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>name</a:Name>
<a:Code>name</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The name is a human readable name of the object. It is only used with objects organized in a naming hierarchy. The simplest naming hierarchy has just one parent (the root) giving a flat naming hierarchy. However, the naming hierarchy usually has several levels, e.g. Substation, VoltageLevel, Equipment etc. Children of the same parent have names that are unique among them. If the uniqueness requirement cannot be met IdentifiedObject.name shall not be used, use IdentifiedObject.description instead.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5534">
<a:ObjectID>91C6BBD2-8A9A-4436-B3EB-4C68B52F5C0B</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>pathName</a:Name>
<a:Code>pathName</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The pathname is a system unique name composed from all IdentifiedObject.names in a standard naming hierarchy path from the object to the root.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o5535">
<a:ObjectID>5FAF38AA-6052-4128-AA50-9450A48A8C60</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>mRID</a:Name>
<a:Code>mRID</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A Model Authority issues mRIDs. Given that each Model Authority has a unique id and this id is part of the mRID, then the mRID is globally unique.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>String</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
