<c:Classes>
<o:Class Id="o6223">
<a:ObjectID>D9AD6F90-0B2D-4FD6-BB77-081DB82D74A4</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Measurement</a:Name>
<a:Code>Measurement</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A Measurement represents any measured, calculated or non-measured non-calculated quantity. Any piece of equipment may contain Measurements, e.g. a substation may have temperature measurements and door open indications, a transformer may have oil temperature and tank pressure measurements, a bay may contain a number of  power flow measurements and a Breaker may contain a switch status measurement. 
The PSR - Measurement association is intended to capture this use of Measurement and is included in the naming hierarchy based on EquipmentContainer. The naming hierarchy typically has Measurements as leafs, e.g. Substation-VoltageLevel-Bay-Switch-Measurement.
Some Measurements represent quantities related to a particular sensor position, e.g. a voltage transformer (PT) at a busbar or a current transformer (CT) at the bar between a breaker and an isolator. The sensing position is not captured in the PSR - Measurement association. Instead it is captured by the Measurement - Terminal association that makes it possible to place the sensing position at a  well defined place. The place is defined by the connection of the Terminal to ConductingEquipment. 
Two possible paths exist:
1) Measurement-Terminal- ConnectivityNode-Terminal-ConductingEquipment
2) Measurement-Terminal-ConductingEquipment
Alternative 2 is the only allowed use. Use of Measurement-PSR and Measurement-Terminal are allowed at the same time for a particular Measurement. Measurement-PSR defines the measurements in the naming hierarchy and the Measurement-Terminal defines where the measurement is placed in the network topology.
</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o6326">
<a:ObjectID>08C432A3-E703-4F73-BA68-A9752B6B1328</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>MeasurementValueQuality</a:Name>
<a:Code>MeasurementValueQuality</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Measurement quality flags. Bits 0-10 are defined for substation automation in draft IEC 61850 part 7-3. Bits 11-15 are reserved for future expansion by that document. Bits 16-31 are reserved for EMS applications.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o6217">
<a:ObjectID>DF90A092-0378-4957-98B0-41290FDC2682</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>MeasurementValue</a:Name>
<a:Code>MeasurementValue</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The current state for a measurement. A state value is an instance of a measurement from a specific source. Measurements can be associated with many state values, each representing a different source for the measurement.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o6373">
<a:ObjectID>D4EA64A7-5046-46A2-9D26-2B307C08BBF3</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>timeStamp</a:Name>
<a:Code>timeStamp</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The time when the value was last updated</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>AbsoluteDateTime</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o6374">
<a:ObjectID>C25BB328-05B6-4253-9614-7F0EAB94EE0B</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>sensorAccuracy</a:Name>
<a:Code>sensorAccuracy</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The limit, expressed as a percentage of the sensor maximum, that errors will not exceed when the sensor is used under  reference conditions.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>PerCent</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o6323">
<a:ObjectID>93CAE303-B8EF-4E31-B09B-FBDE2EBF0B3C</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>ValueAliasSet</a:Name>
<a:Code>ValueAliasSet</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Describes the translation of a set of values into a name and is intendend to facilitate cusom translations. Each ValueAliasSet has a name, description etc. A specific Measurement may represent a discrete state like Open, Closed, Intermediate etc. This requires a translation from the MeasurementValue.value number to a string, e.g. 0-&gt;&quot;Invalid&quot;, 1-&gt;&quot;Open&quot;, 2-&gt;&quot;Closed&quot;, 3-&gt;&quot;Intermediate&quot;. Each ValueToAlias member in ValueAliasSet.Value describe a mapping for one particular value to a name.
</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o6324">
<a:ObjectID>6BC88225-D614-4DCE-BE94-B434DE6381FD</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>ValueToAlias</a:Name>
<a:Code>ValueToAlias</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Describes the translation of one particular value into a name, e.g. 1-&gt;&quot;Open&quot;
</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o6375">
<a:ObjectID>657C1BB2-9A70-4E79-9F7D-73B17D1302A4</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>value</a:Name>
<a:Code>value</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The value that is mapped</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Integer</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o6222">
<a:ObjectID>AA7F4EC9-BFBC-466D-88AE-A990AA576637</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>LimitSet</a:Name>
<a:Code>LimitSet</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Specifies a set of Limits that are associated with a Measurement. A Measurement may have several LimitSets corresponding to seasonal or other changing conditions. The condition is captured in the name and description attributes. The same LimitSet may be used for several Measurements. In particular percentage limits are used this way.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o6376">
<a:ObjectID>9F2A6E3F-14C0-4DE8-91EF-E0D911C7A7BE</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>isPercentageLimits</a:Name>
<a:Code>isPercentageLimits</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Tells if the limit values are in percentage of normalValue or the specified Unit for Measurements and Controls.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Boolean</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o6229">
<a:ObjectID>666A5CEB-4FFC-473F-9524-4ECEE398C6F9</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Limit</a:Name>
<a:Code>Limit</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Specifies one limit value for a Measurement. A Measurement typically has several limits that are kept together by the LimitSet class. The actual meaning and use of a Limit instance (i.e., if it is an alarm or warning limit or if it is a high or low limit) is not captured in the Limit class. However the name of a Limit instance may indicate both meaning and use.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o6224">
<a:ObjectID>581211F0-0618-4762-8073-80733CD3A4B7</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Control</a:Name>
<a:Code>Control</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Control is used for supervisory/device control. It represents control outputs that are used to change the state in a process, e.g. close or open breaker, a set point value or a raise lower command.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o6377">
<a:ObjectID>2BC981B2-FBD8-4391-962C-904EC6771710</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>timeStamp</a:Name>
<a:Code>timeStamp</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The last time a control output was sent</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>AbsoluteDateTime</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o6378">
<a:ObjectID>C2101BD9-3A39-43D5-9792-B67B589FA85A</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>operationInProgress</a:Name>
<a:Code>operationInProgress</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Indicates that a client is currently sending control commands that has not completed</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Boolean</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o6325">
<a:ObjectID>11D40C1E-8DD2-47DD-B14B-FE75D70733E7</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>MeasurementValueSource</a:Name>
<a:Code>MeasurementValueSource</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>MeasurementValueSource describes the alternative sources updating a MeasurementValue. User conventions for how to use the MeasurementValueSource attributes are described in the introduction to IEC 61970-301.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o6328">
<a:ObjectID>DCCF89C9-2B26-4538-B5E6-7971783519EF</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>MeasurementType</a:Name>
<a:Code>MeasurementType</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Specifies the type of Measurement, e.g. IndoorTemperature, OutDoorTemperature, BusVoltage, GeneratorVoltage, LineFlow etc. The MeasurementType.name shall be unique among all specified types and describe the type. The MeasurementType.aliasName is meant to be used for localization.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o6364">
<a:ObjectID>5F2C474E-E982-41D9-947C-A8A11594E878</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>ControlType</a:Name>
<a:Code>ControlType</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Specifies the type of Control, e.g. BreakerOn/Off, GeneratorVoltageSetPoint, TieLineFlow etc. The ControlType.name shall be unique among all specified types and describe the type. The ControlType.aliasName is meant to be used for localization.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o6327">
<a:ObjectID>63F458AD-4CA6-41F8-B863-9B857A4219A6</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Quality61850</a:Name>
<a:Code>Quality61850</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Quality flags in this class are as defined in IEC 61850, except for estimatorReplaced, which has been included in this class for convenience.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o6379">
<a:ObjectID>8EDE69E3-C77B-4EDF-9E99-D6EE8F3490F1</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>validity</a:Name>
<a:Code>validity</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Validity may be good, questionable or invalid. Refer to the Validity enumeration for more details.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Validity</a:DataType>
<a:InitialValue>GOOD</a:InitialValue>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o6380">
<a:ObjectID>9D081BC0-1113-448C-B569-441AE383592C</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>overFlow</a:Name>
<a:Code>overFlow</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Measurement value is beyond the capability of being  represented properly. For example, a counter value overflows from maximum count back to a value of zero. </a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Boolean</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o6381">
<a:ObjectID>B0D2EDF7-0CEA-4164-B7E0-88C39C8567B2</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>outOfRange</a:Name>
<a:Code>outOfRange</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Measurement value is beyond a predefined range of value.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Boolean</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o6382">
<a:ObjectID>5C6E0FF5-B417-415A-B172-D22E3235CB88</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>badReference</a:Name>
<a:Code>badReference</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Measurement value may be incorrect due to a reference being out of calibration.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Boolean</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o6383">
<a:ObjectID>F7FD269B-A52A-42FC-8740-5269E43E00EB</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>oscillatory</a:Name>
<a:Code>oscillatory</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>To prevent some overload of the communication it is sensible to detect and suppress oscillating (fast changing) binary inputs. If a signal changes in a defined time (tosc) twice in the same direction (from 0 to 1 or from 1 to 0) then oscillation is detected and the detail quality identifier &quot;oscillatory&quot; is set. If it is detected a configured numbers of transient changes could be passed by. In this time the validity status &quot;questionable&quot; is set. If after this defined numbers of changes the signal is still in the oscillating state the value shall be set either to the opposite state of the previous stable value or to a defined default value. In this case the validity status &quot;questionable&quot; is reset and &quot;invalid&quot; is set as long as the signal is oscillating. If it is configured such that no transient changes should be passed by then the validity status &quot;invalid&quot; is set immediately in addition to the detail quality identifier &quot;oscillatory&quot; (used for status information only).
</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Boolean</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o6384">
<a:ObjectID>6B95C858-1721-43A7-B70C-85FBB7B7FF58</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>failure</a:Name>
<a:Code>failure</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>This identifier indicates that a supervision function has detected an internal or external failure, e.g. communication failure.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Boolean</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o6385">
<a:ObjectID>0AEBB4CD-BB25-4A93-87D4-A2BB86508AA5</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>oldData</a:Name>
<a:Code>oldData</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Measurement value is old and possibly invalid, as it has not been successfully updated during a specified time interval.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Boolean</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o6386">
<a:ObjectID>4E9AE23C-1903-476C-A04E-13993D7EC701</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>suspect</a:Name>
<a:Code>suspect</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A correlation function has detected that the value is not consitent with other values. Typically set by a network State Estimator.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Boolean</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o6387">
<a:ObjectID>F0A6853B-8385-45A4-AF32-2CB37B7E7F7E</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>test</a:Name>
<a:Code>test</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Measurement value is transmitted for test purposes.</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Boolean</a:DataType>
<a:InitialValue>FALSE</a:InitialValue>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o6388">
<a:ObjectID>FDE91CC2-51F2-45D2-B8E2-9826537E5A01</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>operatorBlocked</a:Name>
<a:Code>operatorBlocked</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Measurement value is blocked and hence unavailable for transmission. </a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Boolean</a:DataType>
<a:InitialValue>FALSE</a:InitialValue>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
