<o:Class Id="o6457">
<a:ObjectID>919B0B98-EA8D-40B8-B508-42BC2690A76F</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>OutageSchedule</a:Name>
<a:Code>OutageSchedule</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The period of time that a piece of equipment is out of service, for example, for maintenance or testing; including the equipment&#39;s MW rating while under maintenance. The X-axis represents absolute time and the Y-axis represents the equipment&#39;s available rating while out of service.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o6456">
<a:ObjectID>9FA08791-63D4-479B-B244-04CDA9643A8A</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>SwitchingOperation</a:Name>
<a:Code>SwitchingOperation</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A SwitchingOperation is used to define individual switch operations for an OutageSchedule. This OutageSchedule may be associated with another item of Substation such as a Transformer, Line, or Generator; or with the Switch itself as a PowerSystemResource. A Switch may be referenced by many OutageSchedules.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
