<c:Classes>
<o:Class Id="o6686">
<a:ObjectID>EE9E430A-8532-412E-B64A-6E60E266C909</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>ACLineSegment</a:Name>
<a:Code>ACLineSegment</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A wire or combination of wires, with consistent electrical characteristics, building a single electrical system, used to carry alternating current between points in the power system.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o6687">
<a:ObjectID>B84EC424-53BB-4818-BD33-D03A248C7812</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>Breaker</a:Name>
<a:Code>Breaker</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A mechanical switching device capable of making, carrying, and breaking currents under normal circuit conditions and also making, carrying for a specified time, and breaking currents under specified abnormal circuit conditions e.g.  those of short circuit. The typeName is the type of breaker, e.g., oil, air blast, vacuum, SF6.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
<c:Attributes>
<o:Attribute Id="o6972">
<a:ObjectID>C8A417AF-EA7E-4B39-803C-6FEA8E8AAFE6</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>ampRating</a:Name>
<a:Code>ampRating</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Fault interrupting rating in amperes</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>CurrentFlow</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
<o:Attribute Id="o6973">
<a:ObjectID>1A1D3008-8641-4402-A3FD-DA09964CF73C</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>inTransitTime</a:Name>
<a:Code>inTransitTime</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>The transition time from open to close, in seconds</a:Comment>
<a:DataType>Seconds</a:DataType>
<a:Persistent>0</a:Persistent>
</o:Attribute>
</c:Attributes>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o6688">
<a:ObjectID>FD9D77F0-1C3C-49E9-BF87-82C29DC8B208</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>BusbarSection</a:Name>
<a:Code>BusbarSection</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A conductor, or group of conductors, with negligible impedance, that serve to connect other conducting equipment within a single substation. 
Voltage measurements are typically obtained from VoltageTransformers that are connected to busbar sections. A bus bar section may have many physical terminals but for analysis is modelled with exactly one logical terminal. The typeName attribute indicates the type of bus bar section, e.g.: Main, Transfer.
</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
<o:Class Id="o6690">
<a:ObjectID>77F8F84A-3EE8-49A0-8EC1-C9628E0AAAD0</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>ShuntCompensator</a:Name>
<a:Code>ShuntCompensator</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>A shunt capacitor or reactor or switchable bank of shunt capacitors or reactors. A section of a shunt compensator is an individual capacitor or reactor.  Negative values for mVArPerSection and nominalMVAr indicate that the compensator is a reactor.</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
