<o:Class Id="o7322">
<a:ObjectID>55C370E1-6C75-43B8-8721-F6B5E4C06FAE</a:ObjectID>
<a:Name>HydroGeneratingEfficiencyCurve</a:Name>
<a:Code>HydroGeneratingEfficiencyCurve</a:Code>
<a:CreationDate>1202478865</a:CreationDate>
<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Relationship between unit efficiency in percent and unit output in MW for a given net head in meters. The relationship between efficiency, discharge, head, and power output is expressed as follows:   E =KP/HQ
Where:  (E=%)  (P=MW)  (H=m)  (Q=m3/s)  (K=constant)
For example, a curve instance for a given net head could relate efficiency (Y-axis) versus MW output (X-axis) or versus discharge on the X-axis.
</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
