<a:Creator>sechin</a:Creator>
<a:ModificationDate>1202478865</a:ModificationDate>
<a:Modifier>sechin</a:Modifier>
<a:Comment>Optionally, this curve expresses elasticity of the associated requirement.  For example, used to reduce requirements when clearing price exceeds reasonable values when the supply quantity becomes scarce.  For example, a single point value of $1000/MW for a spinning reserve will cause a reduction in the required spinning reserve. 
X axis is constrained quantity (e.g., MW)
Y1 axis is money per constrained quantity

</a:Comment>
<a:UseParentNamespace>0</a:UseParentNamespace>
<a:Persistence>T</a:Persistence>
<a:Cardinality>*</a:Cardinality>
</o:Class>
